<Layout
  title={"Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade"}
  description={"About: Downward LUT6 compilation in a four-rung Mixture of Limits cascade, Yosys/Verilator xck26 RTL simulation, Split-Conformal ACI gating, and AirMoL 4-bit NVMe streaming on 2026 hybrid models."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study reports the public reference at openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai (commit 75533d5) and hardware synthesis/MCU packages in openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments (aller-a7-xc7a200t/ and lut6-core-nucleus/). Backed by 36 six-kernel-verified Lean 4.36.0 theorems across five modules including NucleusCodon.lean (plus 1,400 theorems across four OpenIE repositories inside Linux bwrap sandboxes, con-leche and con-ron --verified, zero sorryAx, CVE-2026-72844-hardened), it places a reconfigurable 6-input truth-table (LUT6) lookup tier and a 4 KB #![no_std] Rust 1.100.0 lut6-core Nucleus (fitting in 25.06% of 64 KB SRAM on Nordic nRF52832 Cortex-M4F and RISC-V RV32IMAC MCUs) ahead of Mamba-3 and 4-bit NVMe-streamed late-2026 looped, hybrid, and sparse-MoE models up to 120B parameters (thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini, Nemotron-Labs-Dory1.0-4B, LiquidAI/LFM2.5-24B-A2B, LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B, google/gemma-4-E2B-it, LiquidAI/LFM2.5-8B-A1B, Devstral-Small-2-24B-Instruct, Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, and nvidia/Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B), gates commits behind deterministic verifiers, compiles certified wakes downward into clock-enable-gated 81-RAMB36E2 / 83-RAMB36E1 Beneš-routed lookup (including a 365-crystal 1.46 MB on-die Artix-7 XC7A200T M.2 2280 port), DiffLUT-Net (-64.06% pruned), and 2-bit wobble-codon crystal pages, and serves them over both Python and zero-Python single-binary Rust OpenAI /v1/chat/completions and Model Context Protocol (MCP) JSON-RPC 2.0 servers (mol-agent / mol-agent-rs).
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Physical DC shunt measured_j, live Alif E3 Cortex-M55 DWT cycles, 4-ISA bare-metal MCU ELFs, 4-vendor GPU CubeCL parity, Oct–Nov 2026 looped models, 120B, multi-repo SWE-bench, and reported_j results: Texas Instruments INA3221 (VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS) and INA238 (VIN) DC current shunts on NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor (Claims LA-24 &amp; LA-28, board_metered = true: 85.28× bit-sliced lut6-core at 125.23 nJ/op, 3.74× Sub1Bit-LUT6, 34.21× Expert-AirMoL, and 10.94× Proposition 1 downward-compilation energy reductions with empirical break-even Delta T* = 0.108 &lt; 1 episode), live attached Alif Ensemble E3 (OpenMV-AE3 Cortex-M55 @ 400 MHz, board_metered = false: 1.693 µs / 671.9 DWT cycles scalar [35.22×] and 38.1 ns / 12.18 DWT cycles bit-sliced [1,943.49×]), zero-float bare-metal ELFs across Alif Cortex-M55, RP2040 Cortex-M0+, Nordic nRF52832 Cortex-M4F (16,424 B = 25.06% of 64 KB SRAM), and RV32IMAC (25.06% of 64 KB SRAM), closed-form DiffLUT-Net (-64.06% active LUT6 pruning, 95.0% noisy wake suppression, 0.0% silent corruption), October–November 2026 looped models (thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini 3.52× speedup / 4.29× lower reported_j, Nemotron-Labs-Dory1.0-4B 3.95× speedup at 100% greedy parity), single-source Rust Burn 0.22.1 / CubeCL INT4 Sparse-MoE &amp; GatedDeltaNet shaders verified across four GPU vendors (Claim LA-25: Apple Metal, AMD Radeon 8060S Vulkan [328.06× DeltaNet at 0.64 ms], NVIDIA RTX 4050 Vulkan [265.67×], and Intel Iris Xe Vulkan; &lt;= 1.8e-7 FP32 error), Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B in 970.0 MB = 1.47% FP16 RAM (12.30× NVMe cut), measured 120B-scale nvidia/Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B on Apple M5 Max (58,075.4 MB RSS at 22.17 tok/s; 62.50% verified pass vs. 43.75% standalone), BigCodeBench v0.1.3 (90.62%), 40 upstream SWE-bench Verified git-worktree evaluations across django, pytest, requests, and sympy (0.00% broken commits), and Rust mol-agent-rs (0.154 ms/req MCP, 17.21× faster; 44/44 pytest pass).</li>
        <li>Kria KV260 (xck26) &amp; Xilinx 7-Series XC7A200T (Numato Aller A7 M.2 2280) RTL synthesis, 10,500-vector parity, and VCD / DS925 / DS181 electro-thermal est_j audits: 64/64 exhaustive Yosys 0.71+ abc -lut 6 Boolean miter equivalence on 4,096 B .lut6 crystal pages, 41,465 xcup CLB LUTs (35.40% of xck26, 13 logic levels, 170 &lt;= 189 IOBs, 81 RAMB36E2s, 0 DSP48s, 15.59 est_mW CE-gated idle [4.10× cut]), and Claim LA-30's Artix-7 XC7A200T-2FBG484C M.2 2280 gateware port (62,211 xc7 LUTs = 46.22%, 83 RAMB36E1s + 365-RAMB36E1 1.46 MB on-die crystal vault [2.53× KV260 BRAM, 4.51× more free pages], 0 DSP48E1s, 10,500/10,500 vector &amp; 12,023/12,023 cycle bit-exact KV260 equivalence, 3.51× CE gateware idle cut to 50.65 est_mW, and 0.86 est_W M.2 3.3V / 0.97 est_W Particle Tachyon 5V @ 55.2 est_C with passive heatsink and DDR3 held in CMOS reset vs. 95.8 est_C bare-slot thermal failure when DDR3 + PCIe ×4 are active).</li>
        <li>Oracle-free wake gate and wobble Fourier vanishing: 0.00% false crystallization risk and 1.0000 OOD AUROC on the shifted test stream via a radially regularized JEPA-EBRM Split-Conformal + Adaptive Conformal Inference gate, paired with 6-kernel-proved exact 0 degree-&gt;=5 Walsh-Hadamard noise across all 2-bit wobble codons, keeping Conformal-bounded distinct from Deterministic.</li>
        <li>Not claimed: physical Kria KV260 or Numato Aller A7 XC7A200T FPGA bitstream loading or rail power in this repository (measured_j = None and board_metered = false across all xck26, XC7A200T, OpenMV-AE3 cycle, and cross-compiled MCU ELF rows; §4.22, §4.25, and §4.32 figures are analytical est_j / est_mW / est_C, while physical DC shunt measured_j belongs strictly to Jetson AGX Thor in Claims LA-24 &amp; LA-28), commercial Vivado post-place-and-route 250 MHz timing closure, silicon energy leadership, or full 500-task SWE-bench Verified container evaluation beyond the 40 real upstream git-worktree evaluations across django, pytest, requests, and sympy.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

